WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.030
In 1979, at a medical
school in Massachusetts,

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.710
a new course began for patients
living with chronic pain.

3
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:13.460
Its founder, Jon Kabat-Zinn, had trained
with Zen and insight meditation teachers.

4
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.230
Today, mindfulness turns up in phone apps,

5
00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.240
offices, schools and therapy rooms.

6
00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:21.740
But once the Buddhist
words are left behind,

7
00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:24.080
is any of it still Buddhist?

8
00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.580
In this mission, you'll trace mindfulness
from an ancient path into hospitals,

9
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.610
schools and businesses.

10
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.810
Then you'll hear Buddhists who
welcome secular mindfulness,

11
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:35.990
and others who are wary of it.

12
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.930
Your mission: weigh up
whether mindfulness apps,

13
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:42.110
office courses and therapy
are still Buddhist.
